      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While smart sneakers collect extensive biomechanical and physiological data, there is currently no credible public evidence suggesting consumer models are covertly building psychological profiles from step tracking alone. Manufacturers typically state their sensors track metrics like stride length, cadence, and heart rate primarily for fitness and health insights. However, your concern about data aggregation and privacy is valid, so always review the company's data usage and privacy policy carefully.",
